 2. 🗳️ Democrats&#x27; polling edge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: New York Times/Siena poll ; Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Likely voters prefer Democratic candidates over Republicans in their congressional district by nearly 9 percentage points, a new N.Y. Times/Siena University poll finds.

 That metric is "closely watched by both parties as a leading indicator of political momentum," the Times notes. (Gift link.) 🖼️ The big picture: President Trump's overall approval rating sits at 38%, per the poll.

 Most voters disapprove of his handling of the economy, the war with Iran, affordability and other major issues. 🐘 The other side: A new Reuters/Ipsos poll finds that Trump's approval rating is up from a record low, hitting 35% from 33% after the Republicans' midterm convention last week.

 Reality check: Polls can't fully predict elections, especially given the gerrymandering and map-redrawing efforts in the lead-up to November's midterms that have left few House seats in play.

