 4. ⚾️ 1 fun thing: A softball for the Pope 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Pope Leo and Ron Onesti in Rome. Photo: Courtesy of Ron Onesti During a recent visit to the Vatican to meet Pope Leo XIV, Chicagoan Ron Onesti had to dig deep to figure out what to bring as a gift.

 His choice? A 16-inch softball — a Chicago classic, from a spin on traditional softball, Axios Chicago's Justin Kaufmann reports. 🍕 Onesti tells Axios: "I couldn't bring him a beef. I couldn't bring him a pizza. Giardiniera was already taken."

 "You know, so not a whole lot left." Go deeper . 

 
 
